# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge
We aim to make participation in this project welcoming, respectful, and free from harassment. We welcome contributors regardless of background, identity, disability, experience, or viewpoint.

## Our Standards
Expected behavior includes being considerate, discussing ideas constructively, respecting different experiences, and taking responsibility for mistakes. Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, personal attacks, discriminatory language, unwanted sexual attention, threats, and sharing another person's private information without permission.

## Enforcement Responsibilities
The project maintainer is responsible for clarifying these standards and responding fairly to reports. The maintainer may edit or remove contributions that violate this code and will explain moderation decisions when practical.

## Scope
This code applies in the project's repository, issue tracker, pull requests, and other spaces where someone is representing the project.

## Enforcement
Report a concern privately to the project maintainer using the contact method listed on the maintainer's GitHub profile. Reports will be reviewed promptly and handled with care for the reporter's privacy.

## Enforcement Guidelines
The response will reflect the severity and pattern of the behavior. Possible actions include a private correction, a warning with limits on interaction, a temporary suspension from project spaces, or a permanent ban from participation.

## Attribution
This code was informed by the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1: https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct/.
